  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Four Points Technology L L C recorded $762M in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date. Four Points Technology L L C won 848 awards so far this fiscal year, with an average award size of $898K. Four Points Technology L L C's obligations fell 9.9% year over year. Other Computer Related Services is the dominant market for Four Points Technology L L C, accounting for $736M of obligations. The Department of Veterans Affairs is the largest buyer of Four Points Technology L L C services, with $235M in obligations, followed by the Department of Homeland Security with $153M and the Social Security Administration with $87.1M. Fiscal-year trends show fluctuation in obligations: Four Points Technology L L C recorded $641M in FY21, $618M in FY22, $769M in FY23, $911M in FY24, $845M in FY25, and $762M in FY26 to date. The FY2026 totals are partial and reflect obligations recorded through the fiscal-year-to-date reporting period.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How concentrated are Four Points Technology L L C's obligations by market?",
        "body": "Other Computer Related Services is the largest industry for Four Points Technology L L C, with $736M in obligations. The next-largest NAICS markets are Computing Infrastructure Providers, Data Processing, Web Hosting, and Related Services with $17M and Surgical and Medical Instrument Manufacturing with $9.3M. Several smaller markets together account for the remaining obligations, including Software Publishers at $403K and Air-Conditioning and Warm Air Heating Equipment and Commercial and Industrial Refrigeration Equipment Manufacturing at $859K."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Who are Four Points Technology L L C's biggest federal customers?",
        "body": "The Department of Veterans Affairs is the top buyer of Four Points Technology L L C, obligating $235M. The Department of Homeland Security obligated $153M, and the Social Security Administration obligated $87.1M. Other notable buyers include the Department of Health and Human Services at $64.2M and the Department of Commerce at $59.6M."
      }
    ]
  },
